  "id": "Compound::DB00741 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c8 through a series of mechanistically linked pathways. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortisone binds to Cyp3a7, which then participates in aromatase activity, ultimately leading to the participation of Cyp2c8. This indicates a potential indirect interaction where Hydrocortisone influences Cyp2c8 via Cyp3a7. Additionally, Hydrocortisone is linked to Mometasone, which binds to Cyp2c8, suggesting a direct interaction that may contribute to the observed effects. The presence of a common ancestor, Hydrocortisone, in multiple paths underscores the central role of this compound in mediating interactions with Cyp2c8. The evidence supports a mechanism where Hydrocortisone may modulate Cyp2c8 through a chain of enzymatic and metabolic interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
